= Provenance and revision =

V2 preserves content fidelity while allowing aggressive structural refactoring.

== Source fidelity ==
The live public BITwiki is the authority for inherited public content. Historical design material can explain intent, but it does not override the current public wiki.

== Revision policy ==
MediaWiki already provides revision history. Ordinary evolution should not create title variants such as:
* Revised
* Final
* Final 2
* Styled
* New

Use redirects, archives, explicit historical editions, or page history when those mechanisms correctly represent the relationship.

== Duplicate families ==
Before merging or retiring duplicates:
# compare their content;
# identify provenance and chronology;
# preserve materially distinct information;
# choose a canonical title;
# redirect or archive superseded public pages when appropriate.

== Public repository boundary ==
This repository contains public wiki content and public architecture only. Protected user content, private identity mappings, credentials, internal queues, private configuration, and unpublished operational material are excluded.

== Git and MediaWiki ==
Git provides a developer-readable working representation. MediaWiki remains the live knowledge system and retains page histories, redirects, permissions, and runtime behavior.

